  "publicacion": {
    "titulo": "He co-founded Apple, then gave up his 10% for $800",
    "descripcion": "Ronald Wayne wrote Apple's founding contract and drew its first logo in April 1976, holding a 10% stake. Twelve days later he withdrew: Jobs had taken a $15,000 line of credit, partners were personally liable, and only Wayne had assets creditors could seize. He got $800, later $1,500 more to waive claims. He later sold the founding papers for $500; they fetched $1.59 million at Sotheby's in 2011. $800 in 1976 is about $4,400 in 2024 dollars. Ten percent of Apple's roughly $5 trillion market cap would be about $500 billion on paper, a hypothetical that ignores dilution. Wikipedia notes Steve Wozniak has disputed the exact timing of Wayne's exit. Not financial advice.",
